.TH OLLAMACALLMODIFIER 1 "May 2026" "Adelaide-Lite" "Project-Zephyrine"
.SH NAME
ollamaCallModifier \- Self-Healing Orchestration Proxy for Ollama
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ollamaCallModifier.py
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ollamaCallModifier
(also known as Adelaide-Lite) is a high-signal self-healing tool call proxy that wraps standard LLM API calls. It is specifically built for calling on apps using very small-insignificant models, adding a layer of robustness and orchestrated intelligence. It implements the "Project-Zephyrine Lite" framework, providing semantic memory retrieval, strategic routing, and real-time telemetry blocks. Embrace Hallucination! I mean what do you expect from a very small model, the fuck m8.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Set the port on which the proxy listens (default is 11435).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display a detailed help message and exit.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Orchestrated Intelligence
Automatically routes queries to internal tools (Search, Logic, Action) based on semantic analysis.
.TP
.B Semantic Cache (LUT)
Stores prompt/response pairs with embedding similarity thresholds (0.95-0.995) for near-instant retrieval of familiar queries.
.TP
.B Memory Management
Enforces strict single-model residency in VRAM to prevent system instability on resource-constrained hardware.
.TP
.B Real-time Telemetry
Streams internal reasoning steps directly to the client via <think> blocks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
The host address of the upstream Ollama server.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I response_cache.json
Persistent semantic cache of familiar prompts and responses.
.SH BUGS
If the model outputs an exact match to a cached entry, the cache is bypassed to ensure response quality.
.SH AUTHOR
Adelaide Zephyrine Charlotte (via Project-Zephyrine Lite)
